From 4dcd76c9f873fe0beb657334c73de6d030c03a5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:37:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dnsmasq, wget, iperf3, minidlna, libevent, rp-l2tp, avahi,
 Samba: CVE fixes

- dnsmasq: CVE-2026-93008 (find_soa on a subdomain), -93009 (DHCPv6 FQDN off by one), -93011
  (DNSSEC name buffer), -93007 (TCP slots kept for DNSSEC), from upstream.
- wget 1.25.0: CVE-2026-15146, -58470, -58471, -58472, from upstream.
- iperf3 3.1.3: JSON_read refuses a length of 0 or over 1 MiB (CVE-2023-38403, CVE-2026-71218);
  the server refuses parallel streams, length and window outside the client limits
  (CVE-2026-71217).
- minidlna: the TiVo SortOrder parser stops before its order arrays fill (CVE-2023-47430).
- libevent evdns: the name terminator is bounded (CVE-2026-63387). rp-l2tp: [len], not [len+1]
  (CVE-2026-96891). avahi: CVE-2021-3468 (a client that hangs up).
- avahi wide-area off (enable-wide-area=no, rc/timemachine.c here, rc/services.c in the Let's
  Encrypt commit): CVE-2024-52615 / -52616 are in code that no longer runs; REAPER-FIXES.md T11
  says so.
- Samba 4: Spotlight (rpc_server:mdssvc) disabled, 3 CVEs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
